{"name":"Crimson Glory","hex":"#be0032","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crimson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, slightly bluish red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a deep red colour.","Immodest. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crimson"},{"term":"glory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Great beauty and splendor.","Honour, admiration, or distinction, accorded by common consent to a person or thing; high reputation; renown."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To exult with joy; to rejoice.","To boast; to be proud."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glory"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crimson Glory","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson Glory is an American heavy metal band that was formed in 1983 in Sarasota, Florida. It started in 1979 under the name Pierced Arrow, then Beowulf, before settling on Crimson Glory. The classic line-up consisted of the vocalist Midnight, guitarists Jon Drenning and Ben Jackson, bass guitarist Jeff Lords and drummer Dana Burnell. With that lineup, the band rose to international fame in the mid-1980s and was considered one of the pioneers of the American progressive metal movement, along with Queensrÿche, Dream Theater, Fates Warning and Watchtower. To date, the band has released five studio albums and one EP."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Crimson_Glory_at_ProgPower_Europe_2024.jpg/330px-Crimson_Glory_at_ProgPower_Europe_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson_Glory"},{"title":"Crimson Glory (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson Glory is the debut studio album by the American heavy metal band Crimson Glory, originally released in 1986 on Par Records in the US. It was later licensed by and re-issued on Roadrunner Records in Europe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c3/Crimson_Glory_Debut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson_Glory_(album)"},{"title":"Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson is a rich, deep red color, inclining to purple. It originally meant the color of the kermes dye produced from a scale insect, Kermes vermilio, but the name is now sometimes also used as a generic term for slightly bluish-red colors that are between red and rose. It is the national color of Nepal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg/330px-Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG/500px-California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG/1280px-California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG/500px-California_Palace_of_th